The projection of $\mathbf{v}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$ is given by
\[\frac{\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \mathbf{v}}{\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Hence, $\mathbf{P} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{4}{9} & -\frac{4}{9} & -\frac{2}{9} \\ -\frac{4}{9} & \frac{4}{9} & \frac{2}{9} \\ -\frac{2}{9} & \frac{2}{9} & \frac{1}{9} \end{pmatrix}}.$The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}\frac{4}{9}&-\frac{4}{9}&-\frac{2}{9}\-\frac{4}{9}&\frac{4}{9}&\frac{2}{9}\-\frac{2}{9}&\frac{2}{9}&\frac{1}{9}\end{pmatrix}

